  "notes": {
    "manas-2010:p0315:b001:l018": "Чоң атакең denotes grandfather/forefather here; English avoids adding another genealogical generation.",
    "manas-2010:p0315:b001:l029": "The eight brothers are described as children not yet crawling; the sequence and ages have not been harmonized with the later account.",
    "manas-2010:p0315:b001:l030": "Мас literally drunken/intoxicated; dazed is a contextual rendering of the children’s condition. The reading remains provisional.",
    "manas-2010:p0315:b001:l046": "The printed contrast says ears hear, eyes cannot see. Possible damaged parallel negation is not silently supplied.",
    "manas-2010:p0316:b001:l030": "Каканчым is retained as a possessive-looking Kakan-Chin form; possible witness error for Каканчын remains unresolved.",
    "manas-2010:p0317:b001:l003": "The speaker mentions a prose tale within a verse line. This is not a separately typeset prose passage and remains verse.",
    "manas-2010:p0317:b001:l020": "The house built off to the side is an abrupt image in the witness. Its connection to the surrounding speech is uncertain; the line is retained.",
    "manas-2010:p0317:b001:l037": "Bilerik’s capture is described here in hunting terms. This has not been harmonized with earlier circumstances.",
    "manas-2010:p0318:b001:l046": "Lowercase барбардын is provisionally construed as the place name Barbar in this geographic itinerary. S. Zhumaliev’s study of epic toponyms lists Barbar; identification with a modern place is not asserted.",
    "manas-2010:p0318:b001:l047": "Кутпа is north/northern side in Yudakhin (also a separate religious term khutba). Geographic context favors north. Куюлган, pouring, is retained; the terrain or river referent of this unusual construction remains uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p0319:b001:l028": "Ак үйлүү is a historical ward/hostage institution. Honored ward follows the favorable reception described here; the translation does not establish whether this particular custody was compulsory.",
    "manas-2010:p0319:b001:l048": "The dug-channel image is retained. Укум normally concerns lineage; its application to the channel’s course is contextual and uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p0320:b001:l026": "Мураапы is read as мурапы. Yudakhin gives both inheritance and a supporting kinsman; the explicit kinsman/hero context selects the latter. Printed spelling retained in source.",
    "manas-2010:p0320:b001:l032": "The printed possessive construction Бадышанын Улак кан is awkward; the king’s Ulak Khan preserves it without inventing a different person.",
    "manas-2010:p0320:b001:l039": "Кыям may denote a slanting/sideways route, south, or ritual standing in Yudakhin. The preceding steep path and pass favor a difficult slanting path here. The first-person possessive and where-dogs-perish expression are retained; precise terrain is uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p0321:b001:l004": "What is above has an unresolved referent, possibly upper lands or higher possessions. No object has been invented.",
    "manas-2010:p0321:b001:l023": "This line explicitly identifies Kutubiy as Oshpur’s son. The relationship is source testimony within the narrative.",
    "manas-2010:p0322:b001:l021": "The belt is placed around the neck as a supplicatory gesture. This is not silently relocated to the waist; compare Yudakhin кисе and the Manas encyclopedia entry Кур салуу.",
    "manas-2010:p0322:b001:l022": "Кисе denotes a belt with attached pouches. The neck-belt supplication continues across the display-line boundary.",
    "manas-2010:p0322:b001:l034": "The youngest of six lions is retained, although the earlier genealogy says eight. No numerical harmonization.",
    "manas-2010:p0323:b001:l005": "Ага is contextually rendered uncle: Ulak is the youngest of Karakan’s sons, in the preceding genealogy, rather than Manas’s biological elder brother.",
    "manas-2010:p0323:b001:l044": "The dark ridge and Tal-Mazar are retained as printed. The line does not establish a modern mapped location.",
    "manas-2010:p0324:b001:l008": "The comparison with women is retained as spoken in the epic, without softening or endorsement.",
    "manas-2010:p0324:b001:l026": "The forty-year quantity attached to the costly furnishing is retained as epic hyperbole.",
    "manas-2010:p0324:b001:l028": "The eighty-year quantity is retained separately from the preceding forty-year quantity.",
    "manas-2010:p0324:b001:l034": "Отогот is the gemstone knob worn on the caps of Chinese and Kalmyk officials (Yudakhin), not a plume. Шуру marks beads/coral; маржан таш coral stones. The exact jewelry construction remains approximate.",
    "manas-2010:p0325:b001:l007": "Kaman is retained in the displayed enumeration.",
    "manas-2010:p0325:b001:l008": "Scissor-Ears is retained in a separate display line. It can be Kaman’s epithet, but the source sequence is not collapsed into one row.",
    "manas-2010:p0325:b001:l017": "Forty camel-loads are retained here, without reconciling an earlier ninety-load description.",
    "manas-2010:p0325:b001:l029": "The witness prints capitalized Балтай, rendered Baltay. A possible error for балта, axe, would fit the adjacent axe line, but no silent substitution has been made. This reading needs specialist review.",
    "manas-2010:p0325:b001:l035": "Менде-менде жатабы is obscure. The provisional man-to-man wording preserves its reduplication and question; the precise idiom is unresolved.",
    "manas-2010:p0326:b001:l022": "Калың кымбат is an unusual combination in this uproar context. The costly/weighty force is retained provisionally rather than suppressing the adjective.",
    "manas-2010:p0326:b001:l026": "Жыйылды literally gathered/was gathered; swept away is contextual to the reported destruction, not a correction of source spelling.",
    "manas-2010:p0327:b001:l006": "Жоксон is provisionally understood as destitute/reduced. The rare form remains unresolved and needs specialist lexical review.",
    "manas-2010:p0327:b001:l007": "Айдар evokes forelocks; тул bereft/widowed is retained as bereft rather than introducing a new death not specified in this line.",
    "manas-2010:p0327:b001:l027": "Weather-making is rendered as magic within the narrated battle. No naturalistic mechanism is added.",
    "manas-2010:p0328:b001:l015": "Чунайып is provisionally associated with a lowered/cropped-eared appearance; the phrase remains uncertain and does not independently establish literal mutilation.",
    "manas-2010:p0328:b001:l016": "Iron-rope/net imagery is retained. A troop designation or weapon-bearing sense is inferred from the battle context, not securely identified.",
    "manas-2010:p0328:b001:l017": "The dagger-handed designation is retained contextually for combatants; precise historical organization is not established.",
    "manas-2010:p0328:b001:l032": "Venom from the cheeks is retained exactly as an epic image, despite the following conversion into abundant hair.",
    "manas-2010:p0328:b001:l033": "Five stockings’ worth of hair is retained without reconciling the preceding venom image. Felt in English identifies the stocking type provisionally.",
    "manas-2010:p0328:b001:l037": "The divorced-mother phrase is hostile abuse in reported speech; it is not presented as an independently verified genealogical fact.",
    "manas-2010:p0328:b001:l043": "Теңир урган is an imprecation here: may Heaven strike him. It is not interpreted as divine favor.",
    "manas-2010:p0329:b001:l012": "The ruler’s killing of his own officials is retained. Later repetition is not removed.",
    "manas-2010:p0329:b001:l023": "Жаң-жуң is the governor-general rank in Yudakhin. This plural designation is translated; the next named characters retain the title within their names.",
    "manas-2010:p0329:b001:l033": "Proper names standardized as Ay Jangjung and Kün Jangjung following the shared glossary. Ay and Kün mean moon and sun, but no extra translation is inserted into this verse line.",
    "manas-2010:p0330:b001:l006": "Кынжыдагы балбаны is grammatically problematic. Fretting follows a conjectured verbal connection to кынжы-; the source form is unchanged and the interpretation remains uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p0330:b001:l035": "Бичик is a book/written text used in the scene’s divination. Its contents are narrative prophecy, not historical verification.",
    "manas-2010:p0331:b001:l011": "Ашык көргөн кези экен has an uncertain subject and idiomatic force. Surpassing others is a provisional contextual interpretation.",
    "manas-2010:p0331:b001:l018": "The witness prints уу, poison, where уул, son, could be a lost-letter reading. English retains poison; no silent repair. This conspicuous reading requires specialist review.",
    "manas-2010:p0331:b001:l023": "The witness prints кын, sheath. Чын, true, might be an error repair in this praise sequence, but English preserves sheath. The idiom and reading remain unresolved.",
    "manas-2010:p0331:b001:l041": "Чалыяр refers to the traditional four companions/early caliphs associated with the Prophet; four companions is used without expanding their names into the verse.",
    "manas-2010:p0331:b001:l043": "Sulayman is retained as the prophetic name, conventionally Solomon; the verse’s blessing is not expanded.",
    "manas-2010:p0332:b001:l011": "The approximate sixty magicians and the killing of all of them are retained; the count is not made exact.",
    "manas-2010:p0332:b001:l017": "Көк күбө is contextually a blue armor expression, not the unrelated witness sense of күбө. Source spelling retained.",
    "manas-2010:p0332:b001:l045": "The hero’s striking without approaching is retained as the verse’s claim. A weapon or mechanism not specified in this line is not supplied.",
    "manas-2010:p0333:b001:l018": "Казыналык is provisionally understood as treasury/royal service in the marksman description; an exact salaried rank is not established.",
    "manas-2010:p0333:b001:l025": "Онбашчы is a leader of ten; the numeral is retained rather than replaced with a modern rank.",
    "manas-2010:p0333:b001:l033": "The killing of those who disobeyed is retained explicitly, without euphemism.",
    "manas-2010:p0333:b001:l048": "The dry-stalk hiding image occurs in praise of Karazhoy’s abilities. It may describe concealment behind minimal cover; the literal display line is retained without turning it into an accusation of cowardice.",
    "manas-2010:p0324:b001:l039": "Калдай is rendered governor following the historical administrative rank in Yudakhin and the shared working glossary. The magician in this sequence may additionally bear it as a title; no modern office is implied.",
    "manas-2010:p0326:b001:l011": "Калдай is rendered governor following the historical administrative rank in Yudakhin and the shared working glossary. The magician in this sequence may additionally bear it as a title; no modern office is implied.",
    "manas-2010:p0329:b001:l011": "Калдай is rendered governor following the historical administrative rank in Yudakhin and the shared working glossary. The magician in this sequence may additionally bear it as a title; no modern office is implied.",
